#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:46
msgid ""
"Accepted asynchronous requests borrow their metadata and buffers until "
"acquire-observed `SETTLED`. Rejected admission retains no new borrow or "
"residual hardware effects. Cancellation and deadlines request withdrawal; "
"the caller must continue the required service. Failed drain retains "
"`QUARANTINED` storage and recovery responsibility. The provider detaches "
"actual references before its final release-publication. Consumers, controls "
"and observers must also be joined before their own storage is reused. See "
"the [shared lifecycle contract](../explanation/ownership.md)."
msgstr ""
"Accepted asynchronous requests borrow their metadata and buffers until "
"acquire-observed `SETTLED`. Rejected admission retains no new borrow or "
"residual hardware effects. Cancellation and deadlines request withdrawal; "
"the caller must continue the required service. Failed drain retains "
"`QUARANTINED` storage and recovery responsibility. The provider detaches "
"actual references before its final release-publication. Consumers, controls "
"and observers must also be joined before their own storage is reused. See "
"the [shared lifecycle contract](../explanation/ownership.md)."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:55
msgid "Mapped ownership and coherent Native NOR"
msgstr "Mapped ownership and coherent Native NOR"

msgid "The [public face](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/mapped_storage.h) and [owner](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/mapped_storage_owner.h) use exact instance/slot/epoch loans. Copying a token creates no new loan; epochs never wrap. A live supported CPU/XIP/DMA-read loan excludes every PROGRAM/ERASE writer to the entire aperture. All command, cache and DMA writers must use the sole backend. Consumers join before release. A failed final unmap retains the exact loan for cleanup retry only; joined readers must not resume through the view. The portable owner closes new reader and writer admission, while release and stop cleanup may be retried. Stop permanently closes admission and waits for all maps and the writer without revoking them."
msgstr "The [public face](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/mapped_storage.h) and [owner](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/mapped_storage_owner.h) use exact instance/slot/epoch loans. Copying a token creates no new loan; epochs never wrap. A live supported CPU/XIP/DMA-read loan excludes every PROGRAM/ERASE writer to the entire aperture. All command, cache and DMA writers must use the sole backend. Consumers join before release. A failed final unmap retains the exact loan for cleanup retry only; joined readers must not resume through the view. The portable owner closes new reader and writer admission, while release and stop cleanup may be retried. Stop permanently closes admission and waits for all maps and the writer without revoking them."

msgid "Writer admission checks geometry, alignment, overflow and aliasing against owner, slots, backend context and aperture before effects. Accepted PROGRAM retains its input until settlement; partial effects remain visible and are never replayed. After backend recovery, continued service can retry failed drain. The [Native backend](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/native_mapped_storage.h) preserves caller bytes, programs only 1-to-0, erases to `0xff` and mutates at most the configured byte quantum per service call. It accepts coherent CPU reads only. General serial-memory/SDMMC providers, XIP/cache/DMA qualification and resource factory assembly remain open. The selected H743 reference below does not close those broader exits."
msgstr "Writer admission checks geometry, alignment, overflow and aliasing against owner, slots, backend context and aperture before effects. Accepted PROGRAM retains its input until settlement; partial effects remain visible and are never replayed. After backend recovery, continued service can retry failed drain. The [Native backend](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/mapped_storage/include/nexus/components/native_mapped_storage.h) preserves caller bytes, programs only 1-to-0, erases to `0xff` and mutates at most the configured byte quantum per service call. It accepts coherent CPU reads only. General serial-memory/SDMMC providers, XIP/cache/DMA qualification and resource factory assembly remain open. The selected H743 reference below does not close those broader exits."

msgid "Selected H743 serial-memory reference"
msgstr "Selected H743 serial-memory reference"

msgid "The initial STM32H743/W25Q128JV contract selects exact JEDEC ID `EF4018`, single-line commands, address and data, and both I-Cache and D-Cache off. The integrator supplies reviewed QUADSPI clocks, pins, memory placement and electrical preparation. This is an explicit software reference, not a new Board route or generic serial-memory factory. A source dependency on official QSPI code does not establish physical Flash behavior."
msgstr "The initial STM32H743/W25Q128JV contract selects exact JEDEC ID `EF4018`, single-line commands, address and data, and both I-Cache and D-Cache off. The integrator supplies reviewed QUADSPI clocks, pins, memory placement and electrical preparation. This is an explicit software reference, not a new Board route or generic serial-memory factory. A source dependency on official QSPI code does not establish physical Flash behavior."

msgid "Before an indirect command, the reference must exclude the entire mapped aperture through a checked MPU guard. It must reject an overlapping higher-priority region or an unproved layout rather than let a CPU reader bypass exclusion. Restoring the aperture requires a proved mapped controller and checked guard restoration; failure retains quarantine. The MPU does not stop DMA or other bus masters, whose exclusion remains an explicit external responsibility."
msgstr "Before an indirect command, the reference must exclude the entire mapped aperture through a checked MPU guard. It must reject an overlapping higher-priority region or an unproved layout rather than let a CPU reader bypass exclusion. Restoring the aperture requires a proved mapped controller and checked guard restoration; failure retains quarantine. The MPU does not stop DMA or other bus masters, whose exclusion remains an explicit external responsibility."

msgid "The mapped owner remains the sole writer and controls the complete transition between memory-mapped reads and indirect PROGRAM/ERASE. Every live aperture loan and reader must be joined before leaving mapped mode; cancellation never revokes a map. Accepted writes retain input through real drain, and partial effects are not replayed. Restoring a memory-mapped register value does not prove a readable aperture or erase completion. Unsupported cache/XIP/DMA and other Flash parts need their own admission and final-access proof; the selected reference does not qualify them."
msgstr "The mapped owner remains the sole writer and controls the complete transition between memory-mapped reads and indirect PROGRAM/ERASE. Every live aperture loan and reader must be joined before leaving mapped mode; cancellation never revokes a map. Accepted writes retain input through real drain, and partial effects are not replayed. Restoring a memory-mapped register value does not prove a readable aperture or erase completion. Unsupported cache/XIP/DMA and other Flash parts need their own admission and final-access proof; the selected reference does not qualify them."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:76
msgid "AMP epoch/cache lanes"
msgstr "AMP epoch/cache lanes"

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:78
msgid ""
"The [AMP API](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/amp_ipc/include/nexus/components/amp_ipc.h) and [caller-"
"storage constructor](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/amp_ipc/include/nexus/components/amp_ipc_storage.h) use "
"separate offer and ACK cache lines, exact peer/local boot epochs and a "
"nonwrapping slot sequence. One serialized privileged Thread executes each "
"lane role. The caller supplies storage, coherent acquire/release control "
"access, cache clean/invalidate and a unique hardware-role claim. The "
"configured power-of-two cache granule is 1..64 B and divides 64 B. The claim"
" port rejects a reused or non-increasing local boot epoch, including after "
"normal join. Authoritative nonzero boot-epoch history must survive "
"CPU/whole-device resets and fail closed at exhaustion."
msgstr ""
"The [AMP API](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/amp_ipc/include/nexus/components/amp_ipc.h) and [caller-"
"storage constructor](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/amp_ipc/include/nexus/components/amp_ipc_storage.h) use "
"separate offer and ACK cache lines, exact peer/local boot epochs and a "
"nonwrapping slot sequence. One serialized privileged Thread executes each "
"lane role. The caller supplies storage, coherent acquire/release control "
"access, cache clean/invalidate and a unique hardware-role claim. The "
"configured power-of-two cache granule is 1..64 B and divides 64 B. The claim"
" port rejects a reused or non-increasing local boot epoch, including after "
"normal join. Authoritative nonzero boot-epoch history must survive "
"CPU/whole-device resets and fail closed at exhaustion."

msgid "Accepted send retains its payload until an acquire-observed exact epoch-pair/sequence ACK or explicit proof that the old peer's CPU, DMA, IRQ and observers can never again access the exact lane/payload under that execution epoch. Elapsed timeouts never release a loan; observing a changed peer epoch faults and closes the lane. Restoring an old shared word cannot reopen it. Receive invalidates descriptors and payload before producing a readonly view. The caller joins readers before `finish`; a valid `finish` consumes that view even if ACK cache clean or epoch validation fails, while local state remains retained for retry or recovery. `close` blocks admission; `join` waits for ACKs and finished views; `reset_join` additionally requires exact peer-stop proof. There is no cancel or blocking-wait API. The selected H747 attachment below narrows one multicore reference; it does not supply a general boot or partition policy. Single-core H743 is not an AMP target."
msgstr "Accepted send retains its payload until an acquire-observed exact epoch-pair/sequence ACK or explicit proof that the old peer's CPU, DMA, IRQ and observers can never again access the exact lane/payload under that execution epoch. Elapsed timeouts never release a loan; observing a changed peer epoch faults and closes the lane. Restoring an old shared word cannot reopen it. Receive invalidates descriptors and payload before producing a readonly view. The caller joins readers before `finish`; a valid `finish` consumes that view even if ACK cache clean or epoch validation fails, while local state remains retained for retry or recovery. `close` blocks admission; `join` waits for ACKs and finished views; `reset_join` additionally requires exact peer-stop proof. There is no cancel or blocking-wait API. The selected H747 attachment below narrows one multicore reference; it does not supply a general boot or partition policy. Single-core H743 is not an AMP target."

msgid "Selected H747 external paired-boot attachment"
msgstr "Selected H747 external paired-boot attachment"

msgid "The [H747 attachment](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32h747_amp/include/nexus/components/stm32h747_amp.h) connects the core to an already established Cortex-M7/Cortex-M4 paired boot. It does not launch or reset a CPU, set global clocks or create an MPU layout. The initial reference requires M7 D-Cache off, compatible noncacheable shared attributes and one complete shared reservation kept out of both startup-clearing ranges. Shared wire records, boot words and payloads must occupy that reservation; local endpoint, port and slot metadata stay outside it. Checking only the first address cannot establish the layout."
msgstr "The [H747 attachment](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32h747_amp/include/nexus/components/stm32h747_amp.h) connects the core to an already established Cortex-M7/Cortex-M4 paired boot. It does not launch or reset a CPU, set global clocks or create an MPU layout. The initial reference requires M7 D-Cache off, compatible noncacheable shared attributes and one complete shared reservation kept out of both startup-clearing ranges. Shared wire records, boot words and payloads must occupy that reservation; local endpoint, port and slot metadata stay outside it. Checking only the first address cannot establish the layout."

msgid "Each role supplies a distinct HSEM claim and outgoing doorbell, a serialized privileged Thread executor and an external persistent boot-epoch authority. Reused epochs reject even after whole-device reset. A doorbell is a hint, never an ACK; the existing offer/ACK predicates remain authoritative. Joining an endpoint relinquishes its hardware role claim, not the peer CPU, shared SRAM or external boot runtime."
msgstr "Each role supplies a distinct HSEM claim and outgoing doorbell, a serialized privileged Thread executor and an external persistent boot-epoch authority. Reused epochs reject even after whole-device reset. A doorbell is a hint, never an ACK; the existing offer/ACK predicates remain authoritative. Joining an endpoint relinquishes its hardware role claim, not the peer CPU, shared SRAM or external boot runtime."

msgid "The reference cannot prove that a stopped or reset peer has permanently lost access to an old epoch. That peer-reset proof is `UNSUPPORTED`; a timeout, changed peer epoch or unsuccessful join keeps payload and port storage alive. Applications must not replace this missing proof with a reset-register write or reuse borrowed storage. Physical multicore ordering, cache behavior and board qualification remain independent station work."
msgstr "The reference cannot prove that a stopped or reset peer has permanently lost access to an old epoch. That peer-reset proof is `UNSUPPORTED`; a timeout, changed peer epoch or unsuccessful join keeps payload and port storage alive. Applications must not replace this missing proof with a reset-register write or reuse borrowed storage. Physical multicore ordering, cache behavior and board qualification remain independent station work."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:101
msgid "F407 masked tail handoff and clock barrier"
msgstr "F407 masked tail handoff and clock barrier"

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:103
msgid ""
"The [handoff component](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32f407_handoff/include/nexus/components/stm32f407_handoff.h)"
" reuses the existing ClockDomain barrier. Initialize once, explicitly enroll"
" every owner, close admission, cancel/drain/join all users, stop the actual "
"Platform and release exact leases. An empty foreign domain, stale epoch or "
"retained lease rejects. The domain cannot discover unenrolled users or other"
" bus masters."
msgstr ""
"The [handoff component](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32f407_handoff/include/nexus/components/stm32f407_handoff.h)"
" reuses the existing ClockDomain barrier. Initialize once, explicitly enroll"
" every owner, close admission, cancel/drain/join all users, stop the actual "
"Platform and release exact leases. An empty foreign domain, stale epoch or "
"retained lease rejects. The domain cannot discover unenrolled users or other"
" bus masters."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:109
msgid ""
"The caller enters privileged MSP Thread with `PRIMASK=1`, "
"`BASEPRI=FAULTMASK=0` and `CONTROL=0`. It must establish stopped System, "
"HSI16/reset buses, no active FP/lazy context or MPU, no "
"enabled/pending/active SysTick/NVIC source, no live peripheral/DMA gate and "
"idle Flash with `ACR=0` (ART/prefetch disabled). Rejection preserves masks "
"and writes no MMIO; reading SysTick CTRL consumes COUNTFLAG. The 98-entry "
"Flash vector table is 512 B aligned and fits the exact generated/observed "
"512 KiB or 1 MiB density. MSP is 8 B aligned in `(0x20000000,0x20020000]`; "
"Thumb PC's first halfword lies in physical Flash. Shared device ID `0x413` "
"cannot establish exact-part/PCB identity. The caller excludes NMI/HardFault,"
" debugger and other masters throughout transfer."
msgstr ""
"The caller enters privileged MSP Thread with `PRIMASK=1`, "
"`BASEPRI=FAULTMASK=0` and `CONTROL=0`. It must establish stopped System, "
"HSI16/reset buses, no active FP/lazy context or MPU, no "
"enabled/pending/active SysTick/NVIC source, no live peripheral/DMA gate and "
"idle Flash with `ACR=0` (ART/prefetch disabled). Rejection preserves masks "
"and writes no MMIO; reading SysTick CTRL consumes COUNTFLAG. The 98-entry "
"Flash vector table is 512 B aligned and fits the exact generated/observed "
"512 KiB or 1 MiB density. MSP is 8 B aligned in `(0x20000000,0x20020000]`; "
"Thumb PC's first halfword lies in physical Flash. Shared device ID `0x413` "
"cannot establish exact-part/PCB identity. The caller excludes NMI/HardFault,"
" debugger and other masters throughout transfer."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:120
msgid ""
"Successful tail transfer never returns: it sets VTOR, disables CP10/11 with "
"barriers, clears CONTROL/PSP, replaces MSP and branches while masked. Main "
"SRAM persists until target startup. The target accepts masked entry and "
"resets controllers before enabling gates; no source deadline survives. Image"
" selection, authentication, partitions and recovery stay external. Live "
"RTOS/FPU adoption, H743/cache handoff, DVFS and deep-STOP continuity remain "
"open."
msgstr ""
"Successful tail transfer never returns: it sets VTOR, disables CP10/11 with "
"barriers, clears CONTROL/PSP, replaces MSP and branches while masked. Main "
"SRAM persists until target startup. The target accepts masked entry and "
"resets controllers before enabling gates; no source deadline survives. Image"
" selection, authentication, partitions and recovery stay external. Live "
"RTOS/FPU adoption, H743/cache handoff, DVFS and deep-STOP continuity remain "
"open."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:127
msgid "U575 retained LSE calendar in RUN"
msgstr "U575 retained LSE calendar in RUN"

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:129
msgid ""
"The [RTC provider](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32/stm32u575/drivers/rtc.c) requires an external"
" boot owner to preserve a valid 24-hour BCD calendar, `BYPSHAD`, prescalers "
"127/255, actual LSE 32768 Hz, `RTCSEL=LSE`, `RTCEN`, `LSERDY`, `RTCAPBEN`, "
"`PWREN` and `DBP`. Boot hands over locked WPR; it remains locked between "
"calls with no other writer. Calibration, shift, binary mode, another RTC "
"owner and a live RTC vector reject. Accepted service briefly unlocks WPR "
"with CA/53, checks the protected write and unconditionally relocks with FF. "
"The provider does not write calendar, RCC, PWR or TAMP, enable an IRQ or "
"repair/reset the backup domain. Year-00 provenance remains external; INITS "
"cannot prove it. `set` returns `UNSUPPORTED`."
msgstr ""
"The [RTC provider](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/soc/stm32/stm32u575/drivers/rtc.c) requires an external"
" boot owner to preserve a valid 24-hour BCD calendar, `BYPSHAD`, prescalers "
"127/255, actual LSE 32768 Hz, `RTCSEL=LSE`, `RTCEN`, `LSERDY`, `RTCAPBEN`, "
"`PWREN` and `DBP`. Boot hands over locked WPR; it remains locked between "
"calls with no other writer. Calibration, shift, binary mode, another RTC "
"owner and a live RTC vector reject. Accepted service briefly unlocks WPR "
"with CA/53, checks the protected write and unconditionally relocks with FF. "
"The provider does not write calendar, RCC, PWR or TAMP, enable an IRQ or "
"repair/reset the backup domain. Year-00 provenance remains external; INITS "
"cannot prove it. `set` returns `UNSUPPORTED`."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:140
msgid ""
"ES0499 Rev12 sections 2.2.3 and 2.2.16 identify oscillator-stop limitations "
"for LSE drive codes 00/01 on revision X; Table 3 marks these limitations "
"repaired on W/U. This reference does not qualify a silicon revision, so its "
"crystal-mode profile requires `LSEBYP=0` and conservatively admits only "
"`LSEDRV=10/11` on every revision. It never writes either field. Section "
"2.2.1 separately requires external boot and Board owners to exclude PC13 "
"transitions for crystal LSE on this LQFP part. LSE bypass is unaffected by "
"section 2.2.1 and is outside this selected profile. GPIO reads cannot prove "
"that electrical condition, and this software reference declares no PCB route"
" or measured oscillator behavior."
msgstr ""
"ES0499 Rev12 sections 2.2.3 and 2.2.16 identify oscillator-stop limitations "
"for LSE drive codes 00/01 on revision X; Table 3 marks these limitations "
"repaired on W/U. This reference does not qualify a silicon revision, so its "
"crystal-mode profile requires `LSEBYP=0` and conservatively admits only "
"`LSEDRV=10/11` on every revision. It never writes either field. Section "
"2.2.1 separately requires external boot and Board owners to exclude PC13 "
"transitions for crystal LSE on this LQFP part. LSE bypass is unaffected by "
"section 2.2.1 and is outside this selected profile. GPIO reads cannot prove "
"that electrical condition, and this software reference declares no PCB route"
" or measured oscillator behavior."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:150
msgid ""
"Reads try at most eight coherent SSR/TR/DR pairs and preserve output on "
"invalid or unstable data. Natural year 99-to-00 rollover preserves the "
"domain; successful reopen advances a nonwrapping 64-bit domain. AlarmA "
"borrows one request. Core monotonic deadlines remain independent of calendar"
" time. One service phase per call disables ALRAE with readback and a 100 µs "
"Core-time crossing guard, clears and observes ALRAF, then restores saved "
"alarm registers with readback before detaching and settling. Failed "
"disable/clear/restore retains quarantine. Foreign clock/configuration drift "
"permanently retains responsibility for external recovery. This mode provides"
" no Stop2, LPDMA, VBAT-continuity or wake qualification."
msgstr ""
"Reads try at most eight coherent SSR/TR/DR pairs and preserve output on "
"invalid or unstable data. Natural year 99-to-00 rollover preserves the "
"domain; successful reopen advances a nonwrapping 64-bit domain. AlarmA "
"borrows one request. Core monotonic deadlines remain independent of calendar"
" time. One service phase per call disables ALRAE with readback and a 100 µs "
"Core-time crossing guard, clears and observes ALRAF, then restores saved "
"alarm registers with readback before detaching and settling. Failed "
"disable/clear/restore retains quarantine. Foreign clock/configuration drift "
"permanently retains responsibility for external recovery. This mode provides"
" no Stop2, LPDMA, VBAT-continuity or wake qualification."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:160
msgid "Complete frames and fixed H743 DMA2D formats"
msgstr "Complete frames and fixed H743 DMA2D formats"

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:162
msgid ""
"The [frame contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/frame_stream.h) binds a copied, "
"checked layout to an existing `nx_stream` pool. Audio layouts retain full "
"stored slots, including inactive SAI slots; PDM uses byte-interleaved lanes "
"and complete eight-frame groups. Planar layouts accept up to four disjoint "
"checked stride intervals. These are data contracts, not SAI/DCMI providers. "
"Publication requires complete frame bytes. Empty acquisition increments a "
"saturating underrun counter without choosing silence/repeat policy. DMA-view"
" release requires actual engine, IRQ and peripheral detachment facts and "
"exact control identity/epoch."
msgstr ""
"The [frame contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/io/include/nexus/io/frame_stream.h) binds a copied, "
"checked layout to an existing `nx_stream` pool. Audio layouts retain full "
"stored slots, including inactive SAI slots; PDM uses byte-interleaved lanes "
"and complete eight-frame groups. Planar layouts accept up to four disjoint "
"checked stride intervals. These are data contracts, not SAI/DCMI providers. "
"Publication requires complete frame bytes. Empty acquisition increments a "
"saturating underrun counter without choosing silence/repeat policy. DMA-view"
" release requires actual engine, IRQ and peripheral detachment facts and "
"exact control identity/epoch."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:171
msgid ""
"The [DMA2D component](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32h743_frame_dma2d/include/nexus/components/frame_dma2d.h)"
" has one caller-owned executor and no queue. It admits exact H743 V ID "
"`0x20030450`, D-Cache off and exclusive cold DMA2D. The two request formats "
"are RGB565 copy (the zero value) and fixed ARGB8888-to-RGB565 pixel format "
"conversion (PFC). Unknown formats are rejected; CLUT, blending, other "
"formats and IRQ operation remain unsupported. Both surfaces must occupy AXI "
"SRAM `[0x24000000,0x24080000)`. No Board connection or physical result is "
"inferred."
msgstr ""
"The [DMA2D component](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-"
"SOURCE/components/soc/stm32/stm32h743_frame_dma2d/include/nexus/components/frame_dma2d.h)"
" has one caller-owned executor and no queue. It admits exact H743 V ID "
"`0x20030450`, D-Cache off and exclusive cold DMA2D. The two request formats "
"are RGB565 copy (the zero value) and fixed ARGB8888-to-RGB565 pixel format "
"conversion (PFC). Unknown formats are rejected; CLUT, blending, other "
"formats and IRQ operation remain unsupported. Both surfaces must occupy AXI "
"SRAM `[0x24000000,0x24080000)`. No Board connection or physical result is "
"inferred."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:179
msgid ""
"`x` and `width_bytes` always count source bytes. Source addresses, x, widths"
" and strides align to two bytes for RGB565 or four for ARGB8888. ARGB8888 "
"input on this little-endian MCU stores B, G, R, A bytes; RGB565 discards "
"alpha with no channel or byte swap. Output addresses and strides align to "
"two bytes; output row bytes equal `width_bytes / source_pixel_bytes * 2`. "
"Destination stride and capacity remain bytes. With `LOM=0`, foreground and "
"output offsets count their own format's pixels: source padding divided by "
"four for PFC or two for copy, and output padding divided by two. Each pixel "
"gap is at most `0x3fff`; bits 15:14 are ignored in pixel mode despite the "
"16-bit register field (RM0433 Rev9, sections 18.5.5 and 18.5.20). Width is "
"at most `0x3fff` pixels and height at most `0xffff` rows. Successful request"
" results report output bytes without stride padding. Arithmetic, AXI spans "
"and hardware bounds are checked before acceptance."
msgstr ""
"`x` and `width_bytes` always count source bytes. Source addresses, x, widths"
" and strides align to two bytes for RGB565 or four for ARGB8888. ARGB8888 "
"input on this little-endian MCU stores B, G, R, A bytes; RGB565 discards "
"alpha with no channel or byte swap. Output addresses and strides align to "
"two bytes; output row bytes equal `width_bytes / source_pixel_bytes * 2`. "
"Destination stride and capacity remain bytes. With `LOM=0`, foreground and "
"output offsets count their own format's pixels: source padding divided by "
"four for PFC or two for copy, and output padding divided by two. Each pixel "
"gap is at most `0x3fff`; bits 15:14 are ignored in pixel mode despite the "
"16-bit register field (RM0433 Rev9, sections 18.5.5 and 18.5.20). Width is "
"at most `0x3fff` pixels and height at most `0xffff` rows. Successful request"
" results report output bytes without stride padding. Arithmetic, AXI spans "
"and hardware bounds are checked before acceptance."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:193
msgid ""
"Destination writes and every ownership control must be disjoint from every "
"source-pool slot's full capacity, including frame tails and other free "
"slots. Admission scans the bounded pool in O(n), comparing seven fixed "
"controls per slot. Acceptance borrows the request, exact live source-frame "
"loan and output; the selected source slot remains immutable through final "
"access. Rejection leaves the original source loan with its caller. Submit "
"`SUCCESS` means ACCEPTED, including a subsequent setup/readback failure; "
"such a failure keeps all borrows until service proves drain. The first "
"observed failure remains latched across cancellation and recoverable "
"cache/IRQ guard restoration."
msgstr ""
"Destination writes and every ownership control must be disjoint from every "
"source-pool slot's full capacity, including frame tails and other free "
"slots. Admission scans the bounded pool in O(n), comparing seven fixed "
"controls per slot. Acceptance borrows the request, exact live source-frame "
"loan and output; the selected source slot remains immutable through final "
"access. Rejection leaves the original source loan with its caller. Submit "
"`SUCCESS` means ACCEPTED, including a subsequent setup/readback failure; "
"such a failure keeps all borrows until service proves drain. The first "
"observed failure remains latched across cancellation and recoverable "
"cache/IRQ guard restoration."

#: ../../../../tmp/nexus-quality-20261019/docs/design/io-extension-boundaries.md:203
msgid ""
"Successful completion requires TC and START-clear. Cancel/error drain "
"instead requires START/CLUT/IRQ withdrawal without requiring TC. START and "
"ABORT writes preserve the selected mode. START is a read/set bit: writing "
"zero has no effect. ABORT requests hardware withdrawal without reasserting a"
" previously cleared START. The provider releases the loan only after the "
"hardware proof and clearing FGMAR/OMAR/NLR. Failed proof retains every "
"borrow in quarantine; continued service can recover an actual drain. If an "
"active owner observes its required RCC gate off or DMA2D reset asserted, "
"transfer history is uncertain and quarantine is permanent: restoring "
"registers to zero cannot revoke the borrow, and service, stop or "
"reinitialization cannot reclaim it. An unobserved reset pulse is not "
"detectable; exclusive gate/reset ownership remains a mandatory precondition."
" System-level recovery stays external. Stop closes admission and returns "
"`BUSY` for active work; only after all loans settle does it reset the "
"controller and withdraw its owned gate. These software and ELF checks "
"establish no PFC throughput, latency or HIL result."
msgstr ""
"Successful completion requires TC and START-clear. Cancel/error drain "
"instead requires START/CLUT/IRQ withdrawal without requiring TC. START and "
"ABORT writes preserve the selected mode. START is a read/set bit: writing "
"zero has no effect. ABORT requests hardware withdrawal without reasserting a"
" previously cleared START. The provider releases the loan only after the "
"hardware proof and clearing FGMAR/OMAR/NLR. Failed proof retains every "
"borrow in quarantine; continued service can recover an actual drain. If an "
"active owner observes its required RCC gate off or DMA2D reset asserted, "
"transfer history is uncertain and quarantine is permanent: restoring "
"registers to zero cannot revoke the borrow, and service, stop or "
"reinitialization cannot reclaim it. An unobserved reset pulse is not "
"detectable; exclusive gate/reset ownership remains a mandatory precondition."
" System-level recovery stays external. Stop closes admission and returns "
"`BUSY` for active work; only after all loans settle does it reset the "
"controller and withdraw its owned gate. These software and ELF checks "
"establish no PFC throughput, latency or HIL result."

